enable-local-remote-control-on-daemon-start

Lane: backend

Unit: enroll-local-daemons-for-remote-control

ChildPatch: enable-local-remote-control-on-daemon-start

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Enroll locally managed daemons for remote control and expose their current manual pairing code through protected daemon settings without requiring a TUI client.

Requires: Unit:normalization/route-app-server-runtime-to-harness

Provides: Enable remote control for explicit local start or fresh managed auto-start, preserve existing auto-started daemon policy and internal restart semantics, pair eligible managed daemons in the background, and store only valid current manual pairing artifacts under the daemon operation lock with private atomic settings writes and expiry, stop and disable cleanup.

Boundary: Native remote authentication, enrollment eligibility, transport, cancellation, managed requirements and daemon ownership remain authoritative; unrelated settings survive writes, pairing failure is diagnostic rather than a local-server failure, and no running user daemon or real credentials are exercised during the roll.

Verification: daemon lifecycle tests cover launch features, existing remote policy and restart ownership; settings tests cover replacement, file permissions, expiry and preservation; app-server managed_daemon_pairs_in_background_without_a_tui_client exercises background pairing against a local fake backend.


